<title>UK: Rolls-Royce in $80 mln deal with SAA.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce in $80 mln deal with SAA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering and aerospace group Rolls-Royce Plc said on Monday it won a contract worth around $80 million to supply RB211 engines for two airliners to South African Airways.</p>
<p>Rolls-Royce said the engines will power two additional Boeing 747-400 jets which were due to be delivered in May and October next year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
